## Wine Environment: Game vs Admin — CRITICAL Rule

Two environment functions exist. Using the wrong one causes hangs, crashes, and unexpected UI.

| Function | Contains D3D/GPTK Overrides | Use For |
|---|---|---|
| `engine.environment(for:)` | **YES** — GPTK env vars (`WINEDLLOVERRIDES`, `WINEDLLPATH`, `DYLD_FALLBACK_FRAMEWORK_PATH`, etc.) when `gptkPath` is set | Game launches ONLY |
| `engine.steamCMDEnvironment(for:)` | **NO** | Everything else |

**"Everything else" means EVERY Wine process that is not the game itself:**
- `engine.run()` admin commands (wineboot, reg, winedbg, any internal Wine operation)
- `WineSteamManager.bootstrap()` launching steam.exe for first-run download
- `WineSteamManager.killAll()` — wineserver -k
- `WineSteamManager.stop()` — steam.exe -shutdown
- `WineSteamManager.startPersistent()` — steam.exe -silent background host
- `WineSteamManager.startSteamForDRM()` — steam.exe -silent DRM host
- `WineSteamManager.startSteamForLogin()` — interactive Steam login
- `WineSteamManager.showSteamUI()` — visible Steam window
- `WineSteamManager.sendSteamCommand()` — IPC forwarder
- `WineSteamManager.configureSteamRegistry*()` — reg commands
- SteamCMD (warmUp, installGame, reauthenticate)

**ONLY these two methods use `environment(for:)`:**
- `WineSteamManager.launchGameDirectly()` — wine64 Game.exe
- `WineSteamManager.launchGame()` — wine64 steam.exe -applaunch APPID

**Why this matters:** `environment(for:)` sets GPTK-specific env vars (WINEDLLPATH, WINEDLLOVERRIDES, DYLD framework paths) that load D3D12/DXGI overrides. These must NOT be present during admin operations (wineboot, steam.exe bootstrap, SteamCMD) or Wine processes may hang, crash, or fail to download.

CLI-verified April 2026: `steam.exe` bootstrap with `WINEDLLOVERRIDES=d3d12=n,b;dxgi=n,b` caused Steam to start but not download (package dir stayed at 138 bytes, quiescence-killed after 25s across 4 attempts). Removing GPTK env from all non-game calls fixed the bootstrap regression.

